  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA value remains network-concentrated:</strong> the top chains continue to capture the majority of distributed issuance and often set near-term market direction. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/08/17/u-s-treasury-department-proposes-genius-act-stablecoin-rule\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">U.S. Treasury Department proposes GENIUS Act stablecoin rule</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Institutional expansion is likely staged:</strong> large-scale adoption typically lands on proven networks first, then broadens as compliance, interoperability, and liquidity deepen. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/08/17/compound-bets-usd52-million-new-leadership-team-in-switch-to-institutional-focus\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Compound bets $52 million, new leadership team in switch to institutional focus</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Custody and issuance integrations are moving rankings first:</strong> Chains that win custody and issuance integrations usually pull distributed value share before the broader RWA market total catches up. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/regulation/2026-08-14-cboe-seeks-sec-nod-for-first-us-3x-bitcoin-and-ether-etfs-411879\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cboe seeks SEC nod for first US 3x bitcoin and ether ETFs</a> (The Block).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
